Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"bb557dcb-ac26-4e4f-9959-414c0a8eeb7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4bdac096-b616-314b-8ef8-e922e91e75c9"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"68a2f58c-331e-ad48-8bdc-1c5b55b57a4a"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"53220ee3-6899-434e-920e-60fb530733f2"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"095e4eec-ffd3-a04d-a987-a5fdd486fcf2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"dd22f314-7938-4f4f-8ecc-b332a386f2f1"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a4344c9d-86aa-6741-bb45-59f56a54fb63"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3ba286b5-1e7c-224b-853a-778291db5f74"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e90a0062-0f5f-9a46-9c06-2276b89415db"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0464db35-0166-914d-8c37-28f847fcdaac"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1f5fd311-c3d0-f64c-813d-a0ca8f5a5c79"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"172bf3ff-c8d4-0847-8261-e0efffc7e3a9"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"7e0b4535-8364-f643-bd2a-d0c6a1b6487d"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"00487ea3-650c-7540-825e-0144a25372d9"],

